-- FINDING 4, companion (silent).  A DATE system pin is the instant 00:00 UTC on that date.  TODAY and NOW then
-- localise it into the document's TIMEZONE.  East of UTC (Singapore, +8) the date survives (and NOW is 08:00 on
-- the pinned day, hours BEFORE the 5.00 pm of the Gazette).  West of UTC TODAY is the day BEFORE the pin.
-- A valid-time pin is a plain DATE and is not shifted.
--
-- Printed, with TIMEZONE "America/Los_Angeles" in f04c-... and "Asia/Singapore" here:
--   TODAY under the pin 31 Oct 2012: 31 Oct 2012 (Singapore); 30 Oct 2012 (Los Angeles, f04c).
--   NOW under the pin: 2012-10-31T08:00:00+0800 (Singapore); 2012-10-30T17:00:00-0700 (Los Angeles, f04c).
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 31 10 2012) TODAY
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 31 10 2012) NOW
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (Date 31 10 2012) `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`
